        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "a49acf98-03d6-5a5a-9254-dd43af2c11c4",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Dan Balan, T.I., Rihanna, Jason Geter, Radu Sîrbu, Arsenie Todiraș\n- Organizations: O-Zone, Grand Hustle Records\n- Products: \"Live Your Life\", Paper Trail\n- Places: Moldova, Atlanta, Georgia\n\nFacts:\n- O-Zone was a Moldovan pop music trio active from 1998 to 2005.\n- O-Zone consisted of Dan Balan, Radu Sîrbu, and Arsenie Todiraș.\n- Grand Hustle Records was founded in 2001 in Atlanta, Georgia, by T.I. and Jason Geter.\n- Grand Hustle Records was formerly called Grand Hustle Entertainment and is also known as Hustle Gang Music.\n- \"Live Your Life\" is a song by American rapper T.I. from his 2008 sixth studio album Paper Trail.\n- \"Live Your Life\" features Barbadian singer Rihanna.\n- Dan Balan was nominated for a Grammy as a co-writer of Rihanna and T.I.'s \"Live Your Life.\"\n- Dan Balan is the first and only Moldovan musician to receive a Grammy nomination.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
